# The build context is this directory, and `COPY . .` takes everything in it
# that is not listed here.
#
# Two of these matter beyond image size. .env holds the real GEMINI_API_KEY —
# copying it would bake a live credential into every layer of the image, where
# it survives even if a later layer deletes it. And venv/ is 222 MB of
# Windows-built packages that would be useless in a Linux image anyway.
#
# Render builds from a clone of the repo, where both are gitignored and so
# absent already. This file is what makes a local `docker build` behave the
# same way, rather than quietly producing a different and leakier image.
.env
.env.*
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.git/
.gitignore
README.md
